# Files the Vercel CLI must not upload.
#
# `.vercelignore` matters here because a CLI deploy uploads everything that is
# not listed, regardless of `.gitignore`. The local `.env` holds development
# values — notably `AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000` — and real secrets.
#
# Leaving it in the upload breaks production in a subtle way: Next.js loads a
# bundled `.env` at runtime, and Auth.js reads `AUTH_URL` from it. Because
# `AUTH_URL` is deliberately NOT set in the Vercel project (production should
# derive its own URL from the request host), the uploaded development value is
# the only one present and it wins — so every sign-in on the live site redirects
# to the developer's laptop. Production values come from Vercel's project env
# settings instead; the local file is for local development only.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tool-generated directories (Vercel CLI / coding agents), not part of the app.
.agents
.claude
skills-lock.json

# Local verification scratch files.
verify-*.ts
verify-*.mjs
*.bundle.mjs
